-- title:
--   Inverse-invariance of Haar measure on archimedean twisted centralizers, scalar norm
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra, and suppose the degree $[L:K] = \operatorname{finrank}_K L$ is prime. Let $\sigma \in \operatorname{Aut}_K(L)$ be such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$ (so $L/K$ is cyclic with generator $\sigma$). Write $A =$ `InfiniteAdeleRing K` for the ring of infinite adeles of $K$, and let $c \in A^{\times}$. Let $\delta, y \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K A)$ satisfy `IsNormConjugator`, that is, the image of the scalar matrix $c \cdot 1$ under the map $\mathrm{GL}_2(A) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K A)$ induced by $a \mapsto 1 \otimes a$ equals $y^{-1} \bigl(\prod_{i=0}^{[L:K]-1} \sigma^{i}_{\mathrm{GL}}(\delta)\bigr) y$, the product being taken in increasing order of $i$ and $\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}$ denoting the action of $\sigma$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K A)$ entrywise through $\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id}$. Consider the twisted centraliser $T = \{ t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K A) : t\,\delta\,\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}(t)^{-1} = \delta \}$, regarded as a measurable space with its Borel $\sigma$-algebra. Then any Haar measure $\tau'$ on $T$ is invariant under inversion.
--
--   The assertion is that the archimedean twisted centraliser of such a $\delta$ is unimodular, in the form of the inverse-invariance of its Haar measure; this is the interface needed to compare a twisted orbital integral with an orbital integral at the infinite places. It is used in the archimedean comparison of twisted orbital and orbital integrals for scalar norms.
